Subject: [PATCH 5/8] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 4, patch 5;
 built on 323f92327 with series 2, series 3 and the first four patches of
 series 4 applied): THE OLD LINES THAT CALL ONE MEMBER'S RESULT THE OBJECT'S
 ARE HELD BY NAME (the seat's planted case PV23). The gate held them as a
 count of eight. A new NEGATIVE worded about the object passed when one old
 line was reworded in the same commit: eight before, eight after. THE MEND:
 the eight are named in the gates' file, each by its arc's folder, and a line
 in any other arc fails whatever the count. By the folder and not by the
 number the verdict file gives itself, so a second arc that takes an old arc's
 number is a new arc. The count stays, as the length of the list; the list may
 only shrink, and the gate says when a named arc no longer says it. One test
 of main's changes, with a dated note: the gate's control let a line through
 by raising the count to one, and now names the line's folder. What it does
 not reach: the gate reads a wording. A negative about one member that does
 not use the phrase passes, as it did; whether a claim about the weave rests
 on a thread is the typed rule of WP-0.11 and not this gate's. The lock: five
 tests added to tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py; on the commit
 before, four fail because the gate passes, and the control holds. Tested
 against planted errors, 3 of 3 forms; computed once. 0 of 19.

